08:33:09 said  I rebuilt the BIJZLI Test Series library as a fast static website that matches the original's look and behaviour. At desktop, tablet and phone widths the layout and page heights match, the phone view never scrolls sideways, and a same-browser comparison differed by only about 0.1% — all of it the small "Powered by Netlify" badge, which I left out on purpose because it is third-party branding. Branch, provider, batch and paper browsing, search, filters, sorting, saved papers, activity and all three colour themes behaved identically in side-by-side tests. The remaining gap is that the individual…
